;; world-card-issuers.edn — meisai 明細 worldwide card-company / payment-service COVERAGE REGISTRY.
;;
;; PUBLIC METADATA ONLY (NOT personal data): which card networks / issuers / PSPs / BNPL /
;; wallets exist in the world, their public portal root, and — for sources the member-principal
;; fetch leg has actually learned to read — a statement-shape adapter (:shape). This file is the
;; coverage map the fetch leg draws from so meisai can ingest ANY issuer's statement, not just
;; sumitclub. It is COMMITTED (it lives OUTSIDE the gitignored data/; it holds no statement, no
;; row, no credential, no card number — only the names of companies and where their portals live).
;;
;; `methods/sources.cljc` reads this file and:
;;   - emits :meisai.source/* EAVT datoms (the "data itself in datomic/edn"),
;;   - computes an honest coverage report + an ingest worklist (what is registered but not yet
;;     fetch-adapter-supported),
;;   - resolves a :source keyword to its adapter shape,
;;   - normalizes a raw issuer statement (any currency) into the canonical meisai intake shape.
;;
;; STATUS taxonomy:
;;   :supported     — a fetch-leg adapter + :shape exist; meisai can ingest this issuer today.
;;   :registry-only — known to exist; no adapter learned yet → appears on the coverage worklist.
;;
;; KIND taxonomy:   :network :issuer :psp :bnpl :wallet
;; REGION taxonomy: :global :apac :namer :emea :latam :mea
;;
;; Coverage is intentionally HONEST, not exhaustive: the world has tens of thousands of card
;; issuers. The networks layer is near-complete; issuers/PSPs/BNPL are a representative seed across
;; every region, extensible one entry at a time as the fetch leg learns each new portal shape.
;; Adding an issuer here costs nothing constitutionally; it is public metadata.

{:meta {:version "1"
        :as-of "2026-06-21"
        :adr "ADR-2606122400"
        :note "public coverage map — no statement/row/credential/PAN ever lives here (G2/G3)"}

